v 3
d freeiv: Instrument-free estimation of a linear structural model
d
d  freeiv estimates the coefficient on an endogenous regressor without an
d  external instrument.  Under scale consistency -- the confounder moves the
d  outcome directly by exactly as much as it moves it through the regressor --
d  the second moments leave one number free, the confounder's share of the
d  first-stage residual variance, and the coefficient lies in
d  [gamma-tilde/2, gamma-tilde], gamma-tilde being the OLS slope: exactly the
d  region where the implied variances are non-negative.  The routes impose
d  the same linear structure order after order: the interval (order 2), the
d  quadratic moment estimator (default) and the higher-moment estimator
d  (order 3), the joint GMM on nine moments with its Hansen J and the region
d  where the profiled J stays within 3.84 of its minimum, and its profiled
d  companion (order 4).  For comparison on the same data, judged by the same
d  interval: Lewbel, Schennach and Zhang (2024) as trigmm implements it,
d  Lewbel (2012), the Gaussian copula, the rank control function and Oster
d  (2019).
d
d  Two endogenous variables loading on one confounder switch to the
d  two-indicator model, where the confounder's direct loading is free and
d  identified, so that scale consistency itself is tested.
d
d  Standard errors by the delta method on the moment contributions; pweights
d  in sandwich form; vce(svy) linearizes over the design declared by svyset.
d  Companion commands: freeivmenu (what the data can carry, before any
d  estimation), freeivdiag (what a value of gamma implies), freeivtest
d  (endogeneity, agreement between routes, an outside estimate against the
d  interval), freeivreport (all of it in one table); a dialog box; the
d  examples of the help run from their links (freeiv_examples).
d
d  Four datasets travel with the package (net get freeiv, or ssc install
d  freeiv, all): freeiv_sim1 and freeiv_sim2, simulated with a known truth,
d  freeiv_proxy, simulated with two indicators, and freeiv_card, the Card
d  (1995) extract distributed with Wooldridge's teaching datasets.
d  freeiv_paper.pdf presents the models, the command and worked examples at
d  article length (doi:10.5281/zenodo.22770175).
d
d KW: endogeneity
d KW: instrument-free estimation
d KW: latent confounder
d KW: higher-order moments
d KW: partial identification
d KW: survey data
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Version: 1.0.0
d Distribution-Date: 20261006
d
d Author: Abdelkrim Araar, Universite Laval and PEP
d Support: email aabd@ecn.ulaval.ca
d
